nss_stns resolves users and groups from an STNS API server through the
nsswitch(5) module interface, so that getpwnam(3), getgrnam(3),
getgrouplist(3) and the rest of the passwd and group databases answer with
accounts held centrally rather than only those in /etc/passwd.

It also ships stns-key-wrapper, which prints a user's SSH public keys for
sshd_config's AuthorizedKeysCommand.

The configuration file is the same stns.conf used by the Linux client, so a
configuration can be copied from an existing host unchanged.
